{"name":"Clarity","hex":"#eaf0e0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"clarity","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state or measure of being clear, either in appearance, thought or style; lucidity.","The ability to be easily understood."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clarity"}],"entries":[{"title":"Clarity (Jimmy Eat World album)","blocks":[{"text":"Clarity is the third studio album by American rock band Jimmy Eat World. It was released on February 23, 1999, through Capitol Records, with which Jimmy Eat World clashed several times while recording their second studio album Static Prevails (1996). The band recorded a follow-up with producer Mark Trombino in May and June 1998, and were free to make it however they wanted without interference from Capitol. The recording sessions began at Sound City in Van Nuys, California, before moving to Clear Lake Audio in North Hollywood, California. Clarity, which is described as an emo, pop punk, and punk rock release, marked the beginning of frontman Jim Adkins's tenure as the band's main vocalist, taking over from guitarist Tom Linton."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ac/Clarity_%28Jimmy_Eat_World_album_-_cover_art%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clarity_(Jimmy_Eat_World_album)"},{"title":"Clarity (Sifow album)","blocks":[{"text":"CLAЯITY is the first album to be released by sifow. The album was released under the label Avex Trax on September 13, 2006. It includes the singles CLOVER and LOVE & PEACE. The DVD also contains the PV's for the singles, as well as Jewel."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ac/Sifow_Clarity.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clarity_(Sifow_album)"},{"title":"Clarity (Zedd song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Clarity\" is a song by the German musician Zedd featuring the vocals of the English singer Foxes. It was released on 14 November 2012 as the third single from Zedd's debut studio album, Clarity. The song began as a collaboration with the American musician Porter Robinson and uses a vocal melody written by the American songwriter Matthew Koma. Characterized as a progressive house and dance-pop song, \"Clarity\" was the first top-10 hit on the US Billboard Hot 100 for both Zedd and Foxes, and their first top-40 hit on the UK Singles Chart. It received multi-platinum certifications. In 2014, it won the Grammy Award for Best Dance Recording at the 56th Grammy Awards."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/56/Zedd_-_%22Clarity%22_%28Single%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clarity_(Zedd_song)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/ac/Clarity_%28Jimmy_Eat_World_album_-_cover_art%29.jpg/250px-Clarity_%28Jimmy_Eat_World_album_-_cover_art%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ac/Clarity_%28Jimmy_Eat_World_album_-_cover_art%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/ac/Clarity_%28Jimmy_Eat_World_album_-_cover_art%29.jpg/250px-Clarity_%28Jimmy_Eat_World_album_-_cover_art%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClarity.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Michelle_Chamuel_2014.jpg/500px-Michelle_Chamuel_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Michelle_Chamuel_2014.jpg/1280px-Michelle_Chamuel_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Michelle_Chamuel_2014.jpg/500px-Michelle_Chamuel_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A cover by Michelle Chamuel launched \"Clarity\" into the top-20 of the US Billboard Hot 100.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMichelle_Chamuel_2014.jpg"}],"sounds":{"clarity":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/84/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-clarity.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/84/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-clarity.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-clarity.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/84/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-clarity.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-clarity.wav.ogg"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Strawberry on white background","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Strawberry_on_white_background.jpg/500px-Strawberry_on_white_background.jpg","ratio":1.618,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Strawberry_on_white_background.jpg","share":0.701875},{"title":"Piece of chocolate cake on a white plate decorated with chocolate sauce","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Piece_of_chocolate_cake_on_a_white_plate_decorated_with_chocolate_sauce.jpg/500px-Piece_of_chocolate_cake_on_a_white_plate_decorated_with_chocolate_sauce.jpg","ratio":1.4699946893255444,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Piece_of_chocolate_cake_on_a_white_plate_decorated_with_chocolate_sauce.jpg","share":0.475625},{"title":"Latrobe White House cropa2","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Latrobe_White_House_cropa2.jpg/500px-Latrobe_White_House_cropa2.jpg","ratio":0.787636669470143,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:L